## Goal

Promote the bounded Agent Session / Delegation lifecycle into a provider-neutral CAP foundation while keeping the first physical `chatgpt-temporary` adapter deliberately narrow and explicitly ephemeral.

## Exact identity

- BASE: `90a8e16e6a1badecd3315968339ca691634b7ee4`
- current HEAD: `3f0210a63f4ac225bd74c5e979f87504900505e2`
- branch: `chat/agent-session-delegation-reentry`
- extension execution generation: `121af52763058f651f7d57964d6d5ecfac2a7b12820257d5286fc23bfc781dab`

This PR remains Draft until a fresh exact-head semantic PASS and final target-Windows physical acceptance are current on the same HEAD.

## Preserved boundaries

The generic Delegation foundation remains provider-neutral. `worker_profile` is part of deterministic delegation identity; the first physical `chatgpt-temporary` adapter remains strictly limited to `fresh_readonly_worker_v1`.

- ordinary ChatGPT remains the only current general planner;
- Control Plane / WorkingState / Verification Kernel / Finish Gate remain project-owned authority;
- exactly six public semantic tools remain unchanged;
- no generic scheduler/event bus;
- no same-task automatic parent wake/resampling;
- no nested/fan-out workers;
- no mutating child worker;
- no rich-context/persistent worker implementation;
- no Prime implementation;
- no provider-conversation recovery;
- accepted independent-review procedures remain unchanged.

## Current Stage Research authority

The active first-adapter authority chain remains:

- `AGENT_SESSION_DELEGATION_REENTRY.md`;
- `AGENT_SESSION_PROFILE_BOUNDARY_REENTRY.md`;
- `AGENT_SESSION_PRE_SEND_RESTART_FENCE.md`;
- `AGENT_SESSION_TEMPORARY_EPHEMERAL_REENTRY.md`;
- `AGENT_SESSION_TEMPORARY_BOOTSTRAP_LIFETIME_REENTRY.md`;
- `AGENT_SESSION_TEMPORARY_PREFLIGHT_COMMIT_REENTRY.md`;
- `AGENT_SESSION_TEMPORARY_PREFLIGHT_OWNER_REBIND_REENTRY.md`;
- `AGENT_SESSION_TEMPORARY_PROMPT_SOURCE_PROVENANCE_REENTRY.md`;
- `AGENT_SESSION_TEMPORARY_LOOPBACK_AUTH_REENTRY.md`.

The top-level decision remains **NARROW**. `fresh_readonly_worker_v1` is an ephemeral one-shot independence profile, not a persistent Agent Session.

## Current Temporary Chat contract

```text
prepared/open generic delegation
 -> neutral ChatGPT preflight
 -> exact archived/runtime-attested MV3 worker
 -> authenticated loopback controller binding
 -> exact live composer == intended worker prompt
 -> fresh/non-personalized/no-plugin qualification
 -> one IndexedDB browser claim
 -> one project-local claim
 -> exactly one Send authority
 -> exact composer synchronous recheck immediately before click
 -> post-Send exact whole-line correlation proof
 -> delivered | unknown
 -> cleanup/capture only while exactly one live/current composer is proven clean
 -> exact correlated WORKER_RESULT_V1 capture
```

The private durable `run_id` remains absent from task/browser-history URL state, worker prompt and IndexedDB delivery claim. Complete browser/MV3 lifetime loss remains fail closed and cannot reconstruct Send/monitor authority.

## Exact source execution contract

Physical qualification continues to execute only exact archived/runtime-attested bytes from a clean exact HEAD, with SHA locking, exact extension attestation, Python `-I -B -S`, authenticated pinned loopback ownership and post-result provenance revalidation.

## Latest fresh-review findings and closure

Fresh ordinary-ChatGPT review of exact HEAD `89458adc6bed5e27faaa5e2b52f15625850b943b` returned `FINDINGS` with two concrete issues. That review is historical after the material fixes below.

### P1 — malformed/prefix/suffix post-Send marker matches

Root cause: post-Send delivery recognition used substring `includes(...)`, so malformed or prefixed/suffixed marker lines could project to the expected correlation; multiple correlated candidate user turns were not rejected.

Current closure:

- correlation is parsed as exact whole lines for exactly one `WORKER_TASK_V1`, `delegation_id=<exact>`, `delivery_id=<exact>` and `task_sha256=<exact>`;
- provider UI decoration such as `Развернуть` / `Expand` may exist on unrelated lines;
- malformed, prefixed, suffixed, missing or duplicate correlation marker lines fail closed;
- multiple correlated candidate user turns fail closed;
- one unrelated ordinary user turn plus one exact correlated decorated turn remains acceptable;
- both `content.js` delivery visibility and the independent post-delivery guard use the same strengthened policy mechanism;
- pre-Send full exact prompt equality and the synchronous immediate-pre-click exact check remain unchanged;
- exactly one `button.click()` Send path remains.

Adversarial runtime coverage exercises provider decoration, suffix/prefix collisions, duplicate/missing markers, multiple exact/malformed candidates and wrong correlation.

### P2 — hidden/stale composer could prove cleanup/capture clean

Root cause: the post-delivery guard selected the first global `#prompt-textarea`/fallback without the live/visible/scope/single-candidate protections already used before Send.

Current closure:

- post-delivery composer selection now requires a connected visible eligible editor;
- `aria-hidden` and disabled/ineligible editors are rejected;
- the editor must belong to a visible `form`;
- exactly one live/current editor must exist; multiple live candidates are ambiguous and fail closed;
- hidden/stale empty editors cannot mask an active dirty editor;
- cleanup/capture authorization synchronously rechecks the stronger current composer guard;
- focused runtime tests cover hidden stale + active dirty, hidden stale + active empty, multiple live editors, aria-hidden editor and ownerless editor.

Existing synthetic post-delivery fixtures were updated only to model the stronger qualified live-composer shape; this does not weaken runtime semantics.

## Failure-class closure

The repository method remains:

```text
Finding -> Root Cause -> Failure Class -> Repository-wide Search -> Guard
```

The P1 substring/candidate-ambiguity class is closed centrally in policy and exercised behaviorally. The P2 stale/hidden/multiple-editor class reuses the already established live-editor invariant rather than adding a new authority framework.

## Execution generation

The material `policy.js` runtime change moved the extension execution generation to:

`121af52763058f651f7d57964d6d5ecfac2a7b12820257d5286fc23bfc781dab`

The generation binding test is green on the current exact HEAD.

## Hosted CI — exact current HEAD

All required hosted workflows are green on exact HEAD `3f0210a63f4ac225bd74c5e979f87504900505e2`:

- Direct Semantic Tunnel Acceptance — PASS, run `34028818648`;
- CodeQL Security — PASS, run `34028818673`;
- Stage 26.3A Six-Tool Semantic Acceptance — PASS, run `34028818655`;
- Semantic Projection Acceptance — PASS, run `34028818678`;
- Stage 26.3B Windows Application L3 Acceptance — PASS, run `34028818660`;
- `ci` — PASS, run `34028818647`;
- Stage 25.1 Vision Runtime Acceptance — PASS, run `34028818645`;
- Secret History Scan — PASS, run `34028818684`.

The final `ci` run includes the complete Python unit/contract suite with the new P1/P2 adversarial runtime regressions.

## Acceptance remaining

1. run a genuinely fresh ordinary-ChatGPT semantic review on exact BASE `90a8e16e6a1badecd3315968339ca691634b7ee4` / HEAD `3f0210a63f4ac225bd74c5e979f87504900505e2` using BASE `code-review` v1.1;
2. independently validate any surviving finding; any material source fix moves HEAD and invalidates that review;
3. only after exact-head semantic PASS, rerun target-Windows / ordinary-Chat physical qualification on the same reviewed HEAD:
   - A normal run: exactly one Send -> delivered -> genuine correlated `WORKER_RESULT_V1` captured/recorded;
   - B1 pre-first-claim complete Chrome loss: zero browser claim/controller/Send authority after lifetime loss;
   - B2 post-claim complete Chrome loss: zero second Send and exact fail-closed durable state unless result was already recorded;
4. re-resolve BASE/HEAD unchanged, keep exact-head CI current, mark ready and merge only while review/physical/CI evidence remains current.

Persistent ordinary-ChatGPT conversation identity, browser wake and cross-restart Existing-Session Delivery remain separate future research after #149.

